<div style="width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(56px,10vh,120px) clamp(20px,5vw,56px) 0;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(83% 0.05 80);margin:0 0 24px;">Our approach · Insights</p><h1 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,5.4vw,72px);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin:0 0 32px;max-width:18ch;">We don’t start with your brand. We start with your business.</h1><p style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(88% 0.015 60);margin:0;">DsignPoint · November 2026 · 5 min read</p></div>
</section>
<section style="background:oklch(97% 0.012 70);padding:clamp(32px,5vh,64px) 0 0;"><div style="width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,56px);"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;aspect-ratio:16/8;"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="../../uploads/ins_start.webp" alt="A notebook with hand-drawn sketches, coffee and glasses on a sunlit terrace table by the sea" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 70%;"></div></div></section>
<section style="background:oklch(97% 0.012 70);padding:clamp(48px,8vh,88px) 0 clamp(64px,10vh,120px);"><div class="art" style="width:100%;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,56px);"><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,30px);line-height:1.4;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 44px;">Most conversations with an agency begin the same way. A founder arrives with a request: a new website, a logo, some social media, better SEO. It sounds clear and reasonable. It is also, very often, the wrong place to start.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">A request is usually a symptom</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">When someone asks for a new website, they are rarely asking for a website. They are telling us that something about how their business shows up no longer feels right. The real cause can sit somewhere else entirely.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">A website request may be a positioning problem. A social media request may be an offer problem. A request for more leads may be a conversion problem. A rebrand request may be a sign that the business has evolved and nothing around it has caught up. Build exactly what was asked for, and the underlying issue stays where it was, now with a nicer wrapper.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Take PadelCreations, a padel court builder. On the surface it was a website project. Underneath, heavy code and bloated media had slowed every page, rankings had dropped, and visitors struggled to find their way around. A fresh design alone would have changed none of that, so we began with technical health and the structure of the site, and designed on top. <a href="../../case-studies/padelcreations/" style="color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);border-bottom:1px solid oklch(33% 0.14 17);white-space:nowrap;">See the PadelCreations case study →</a></p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">The first question we ask</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">So we don’t begin with “What service do you want?” We begin with three questions, asked together:</p><div style="background:oklch(93% 0.015 60);padding:clamp(28px,4vw,52px);margin:40px 0;"><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);margin:0;">Where is your business today, where are you trying to go, and what is preventing you from getting there?</p></div><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">The answers shape everything that follows. They tell us whether the business needs a clearer position, a sharper offer, a better journey for its customers, a stronger digital presence, or a combination of these.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Skipping this step feels faster. It rarely is. A website built on unclear positioning has to be rebuilt once the positioning is clarified. A campaign for an offer that is hard to explain spends its budget teaching people what you do. Diagnosis first costs a little time up front and saves a lot of it later.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">What a diagnosis actually looks at</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Before we recommend anything, we look at the business as a whole: the model, the audience, the positioning and the offer, the messaging, the customer journey, the website, and how leads arrive and convert. We also look at what is already working, because there is usually more of it than the founder gives themselves credit for.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">When JD Assist opened a professional academy, the diagnosis showed that it needed neither a big brand project nor a large website first. It needed a way to turn early interest into real prospects. So we built one funnel around two simple actions, joining the waiting list or downloading a guide. <a href="../../case-studies/jd-assist/" style="color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);border-bottom:1px solid oklch(33% 0.14 17);white-space:nowrap;">See the JD Assist case study →</a></p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">The outcome is not a long report. It is clarity: where the business stands, what is in the way, what should happen first, what can wait, and what does not need to happen at all.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Sometimes the answer is to change nothing</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">This is the part that surprises people. If your website already works, we won’t tell you to rebuild it. If your brand still fits where you are going, we won’t tell you to reinvent it. If you don’t need social media this quarter, we won’t invent work to fill a calendar.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">No unnecessary reinvention. No design for the sake of design. No marketing for the sake of marketing. The aim is the right intervention at the right moment.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Capabilities, not a menu</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">We do have specialist skills in positioning, brand, websites, SEO, content, automation and AI. But they aren’t a menu to choose from. They are tools, and the diagnosis decides which ones the business needs and in what order. Strategy determines what gets built, so we never build first and ask questions later.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">A business that has outgrown its positioning may need diagnosis, messaging, a brand evolution and a restructured website, working together. One launching a new offer may need offer strategy, a landing page and a lead-generation system. The scope comes from the diagnosis, never from a predefined package.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Progress, not deliverables</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">A traditional agency relationship ends when the deliverable ships. Ours is built around progress: diagnosis, strategy, priorities, implementation and, where it makes sense, an ongoing partnership that keeps asking what the business should do next. We would rather be the person you call when you are wondering whether to rebrand, launch an offer or enter a new market than the supplier you email when you need twelve posts.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Who this is for</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Founders and established service businesses that have reached a new stage. The brand feels outdated, or the offer has become complicated. The website undersells the business. Marketing is busy but nothing seems to move. Or the founder simply knows that something has to change without being sure what.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">What you’ll find here</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Insights is where we share how we think. Expect practical notes on positioning, brand, websites and growth, written for founders whose business has reached a point where what worked before is no longer enough for where it is going.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">If that sounds like you, you are in the right place. And if you would rather talk it through, we are always happy to.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:44px 0 0;">Not sure where your business stands? <a href="../../book-a-call/" style="color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);border-bottom:1px solid oklch(33% 0.14 17);">Tell us where you are today</a> and we’ll help you see it clearly.</p></div></section>
<section style="background:oklch(93% 0.015 60);padding:clamp(56px,9vh,100px) 0;"><div style="width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,56px);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:clamp(24px,4vw,64px);align-items:center;"><a class="img-z" href="../outgrown-your-brand/" style="flex:1 1 360px;aspect-ratio:4/3;"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="../../uploads/ins_outgrown.webp" alt="Old printed brand materials beside fresh burgundy and champagne colour swatches on a sunlit table" style="object-position:center 62%;"></a><div style="flex:1 1 360px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 24px;">Keep reading</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,46px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin:0 0 18px;"><a class="ttl" href="../outgrown-your-brand/">Have you outgrown your brand?</a></h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 28px;max-width:44ch;">Your brand wasn’t wrong when you built it. But the business may have moved on. Six signs the gap is real, and what to do before you commission anything.</p><a class="rd" href="../outgrown-your-brand/">Read the article <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
